GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `amended annex ד' row`
DECIDE `the amended annex ד' row for` y m IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the retirement year` EQUALS y AND r's `the retirement month` EQUALS m) `the rows of the amended annex ד'`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST r

§§ `illustrations`

-- (א)–(ג): the frame of four years is 7.25%, the figure 5.1.4 completes
-- to; for a body outside amendment 50, 7.25% less 2009's 1.7857% — the
-- figure 5.1.4's deduction leaves from 1.7.2013. The recital's period now
-- ends where the framework's §2 does.
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework cost frame in all, as amended` TRUE EQUALS `the allocation 5.1.4 completes to`
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` `the day 5.1.4 completes the allocation from` TRUE EQUALS `the 2011 framework cost frame in all, as amended` TRUE
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` `the day 5.1.4 completes the allocation from` FALSE EQUALS `the 2011 framework cost frame in all, as amended` FALSE
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012) TRUE EQUALS 4%
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) TRUE EQUALS 6.25%
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) FALSE EQUALS 4.4643%
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012) FALSE EQUALS 2.25%
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2011) FALSE EQUALS 2.25%
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2010) TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `in the 2011 framework agreement's period` `the 2011 framework's cost frame period ends, as amended, on`
#ASSERT NOT `in the 2011 framework agreement's period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2013)
#ASSERT `the agreement the 2011 amendment amends was signed on` `is on or before` `the 2011 amendment was signed on`

-- F-framework-2011-amendment-a's evidence: from 1.1.2012 the cost 5.1.4
-- deducts is more than 5.1.2's completion, the only one by then, and
-- deducted from it as printed it would take the allocation below 5.1.1's
-- 2.25%, which 5.1.1 gives those bodies too.
`the 1.7857% deduction is more than 5.1.2's completion` MEANS
        `the cost 5.1.4 deducts for a body outside amendment 50` GREATER THAN `the allocation 5.1.2 completes to, as amended` MINUS `the 2011 supplement's first rate`
    AND `the allocation 5.1.2 completes to, as amended` MINUS `the cost 5.1.4 deducts for a body outside amendment 50` LESS THAN `the 2011 framework allocation on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2011) FALSE
#ASSERT `the 1.7857% deduction is more than 5.1.2's completion`

-- §10: where no agreement allocates any step, the supplement reaches §5's
-- allocation on each day: 4% in 2012, 6.25% in 2013, 7.25% from 1.7.2013;
-- 2.25% before 2012, as the framework has it. One allocated step leaves
-- its share out.
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement's rate as amended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2011) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 2.25%
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement's rate as amended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012) TRUE
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement's rate as amended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) TRUE
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement's rate as amended on` `the day 5.1.4 completes the allocation from` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` `the day 5.1.4 completes the allocation from` TRUE
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement's rate as amended on` `the day 5.1.4 completes the allocation from` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 5.5%
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement's rate as amended on` `the day 5.1.4 completes the allocation from` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS 2.25%
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement's rate as amended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 2.25%
-- 10.6: the special scales' tables stand at 100% plus §5's allocation on
-- each day; the judges' typists' basic salary takes the whole frame.
#ASSERT `the share of their table a special scale is paid on, as amended` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012) MINUS 100% EQUALS `the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012) TRUE
#ASSERT `the share of their table a special scale is paid on, as amended` `the day 5.1.4 completes the allocation from` MINUS 100% EQUALS `the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` `the day 5.1.4 completes the allocation from` TRUE
#ASSERT `the share of their table a special scale is paid on, as amended` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2011) EQUALS 102.25%
#ASSERT `the cost the judges' typists' basic salary takes, as amended` EQUALS `the 2011 framework cost frame in all, as amended` TRUE

-- §14: a retiree of March 2013 is eligible now; one of July 2013 is not.
-- Retired in June 2012, 10,000: column C from 2013 (2.1[לא קריא]% — no
-- answer); retired in September 2012: column C from 2013 and D on top from
-- July 2013; retired in June 2010: as the framework had it in 2012.
#ASSERT `an eligible retiree under §14.1.1 as amended` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2013) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `an eligible retiree under §14.1.1` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2013) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `an eligible retiree under §14.1.1 as amended` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2013) TRUE
#ASSERT `the determining salary raised under §14 as amended for` 10000 2012 9 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) EQUALS JUST (10000 TIMES (1 PLUS 2.1635%))
#ASSERT `the determining salary raised under §14 as amended for` 10000 2012 9 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2013) EQUALS JUST (10000 TIMES (1 PLUS 2.1635%) TIMES (1 PLUS 0.4706%))
#ASSERT `the determining salary raised under §14 as amended for` 10000 2012 9 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012) EQUALS JUST 10000
#ASSERT `the determining salary raised under §14 as amended for` 10000 2012 6 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the determining salary raised under §14 as amended for` 10000 2012 6 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012) EQUALS JUST 10000
#ASSERT `the determining salary raised under §14 as amended for` 10000 2010 6 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012) EQUALS `the determining salary raised under §14 for` 10000 2010 6 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012)
#ASSERT `the determining salary raised under §14 as amended for` 10000 2013 6 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2013) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the determining salary raised under §14 as amended for` 10000 2009 1 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2011) EQUALS `the determining salary raised under §14 for` 10000 2009 1 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2011)
#ASSERT count `the rows of the amended annex ד'` EQUALS 53
-- One who retired in March 2011 is raised by C from 2013 now; the
-- framework's annex gave that month no C.
#ASSERT `the determining salary raised under §14 as amended for` 10000 2011 3 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) EQUALS JUST (10000 TIMES (1 PLUS 1.7115%) TIMES (1 PLUS 0.0172%))

-- The amended annex ד' against the text. (1) Every cell the corpus reads
-- is above nothing exactly in its column's months of retirement, the
-- periods of 14.1.3.1–14.1.3.4 as amended (C from March 2011, D from July
-- 2012). (2) Column A, and column B before March 2011, are the
-- framework's annex's where both read. (3) Each column's last figure is
-- its step of §5 as amended over a salary the allocation before it has
-- already raised, to four places: B 1.75% over 102.25%, C 2.25% over 104%,
-- D 1% over 106.25%; and column D climbs to it by sixths over July–December
-- 2012.
GIVEN cell IS A MAYBE NUMBER, r IS AN `amended annex ד' row`, p IS AN `amended annex ד' column period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a cell keeps to its column's period` cell r p IF
    CONSIDER cell
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST c THEN IF c GREATER THAN 0 THEN within ELSE NOT within
    WHERE
        first MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (r's `the retirement month`) (r's `the retirement year`)
        within MEANS     first `is on or after` (p's `its first retirement day`)
                     AND first `is on or before` (p's `its last retirement day`)

GIVEN r IS AN `amended annex ד' row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the row keeps each column to its period` r IF
        `a cell keeps to its column's period` (r's `column A as amended`) r `column A's period`
    AND `a cell keeps to its column's period` (r's `column B as amended`) r `column B's period`
    AND `a cell keeps to its column's period` (r's `column C as amended`) r `column C's period, as amended`
    AND `a cell keeps to its column's period` (r's `column D as amended`) r `column D's period`

#ASSERT all `the row keeps each column to its period` `the rows of the amended annex ד'`

GIVEN r IS AN `amended annex ד' row`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the month count of` r IS
    (r's `the retirement year` TIMES 12) PLUS r's `the retirement month`

`the month count of March 2011` MEANS (2011 TIMES 12) PLUS 3

GIVEN new IS A MAYBE NUMBER, old IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cells agree where both read` new old IF
    CONSIDER new
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST n THEN CONSIDER old
                     WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                     WHEN JUST o THEN n EQUALS o

GIVEN r IS AN `amended annex ד' row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the row's A, and B before March 2011, are the framework's` r IF
    CONSIDER `the annex ד' row for` (r's `the retirement year`) (r's `the retirement month`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST o THEN     `the cells agree where both read` (r's `column A as amended`) (JUST (o's `column A`))
                     AND (   `the month count of` r AT LEAST `the month count of March 2011`
                          OR `the cells agree where both read` (r's `column B as amended`) (JUST (o's `column B`)))

#ASSERT all `the row's A, and B before March 2011, are the framework's` `the rows of the amended annex ד'`

GIVEN `the step's day` IS A DATE, `the day before it` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a step of §5 as amended over the salary before it` `the step's day` `the day before it` IS
    ((`the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` `the step's day` TRUE MINUS before) DIVIDED BY (1 PLUS before)) `to the nearest` 0.000001
    WHERE
        before MEANS `the 2011 framework allocation as amended on` `the day before it` TRUE

`column B's last figure` MEANS `a step of §5 as amended over the salary before it` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2012) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2011)
`column C's last figure` MEANS `a step of §5 as amended over the salary before it` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2013) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2012)
`column D's last figure` MEANS `a step of §5 as amended over the salary before it` `the day 5.1.4 completes the allocation from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2013)

GIVEN r IS AN `amended annex ד' row`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the months from June 2012 to the row` r IS
    (r's `the retirement year` MINUS 2012) TIMES 12 PLUS r's `the retirement month` MINUS 6

GIVEN r IS AN `amended annex ד' row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the row's last figures are the steps of §5` r IF
        (   `the month count of` r LESS THAN `the month count of March 2011`
         OR r's `the retirement year` AT LEAST 2012
         OR `the cells agree where both read` (r's `column B as amended`) (JUST `column B's last figure`))
    AND (   `the months from June 2012 to the row` r LESS THAN 1
         OR r's `the retirement year` AT LEAST 2013
         OR `the cells agree where both read` (r's `column C as amended`) (JUST `column C's last figure`))
    AND (   `the months from June 2012 to the row` r LESS THAN 1
         OR `the cells agree where both read` (r's `column D as amended`) (JUST (((min (`the months from June 2012 to the row` r) 6) TIMES `column D's last figure` DIVIDED BY 6) `to the nearest` 0.000001)))

#ASSERT all `the row's last figures are the steps of §5` `the rows of the amended annex ד'`
#ASSERT `column B's last figure` EQUALS 1.7115%
#ASSERT `column C's last figure` EQUALS 2.1635%
#ASSERT `column D's last figure` EQUALS 0.9412%
